  "final_text": "All four steps are done, and the read-back confirms the rule is enabled and the panel title changed.\n\n- **Data view:** The time field of \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" is `timestamp`.\n- **Dashboard:** \"S4-b3ae9bc7 Web logs\" has two panels: \"Requests over time\" and \"Requests by response code\".\n- **Alert rule:** \"S4-b3ae9bc7 5xx errors\" checks every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests with a response code from 500 to 599 arrive within 5 minutes. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n- **Panel edit:** The second panel is now titled \"Responses by code\".\n- **Read-back:** The rule shows `enabled: true` with status `ok`.\n\nThe `response` field is a string, so the rule matches 500\u2013599 as a text range on `response.keyword`. That works for three-digit codes. I haven't tested the rule against real 5xx data.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
